{"name":"Tinsmith","hex":"#dce0dc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tinsmith","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who makes or repairs things with tin or similar alloys.","A dealer in tin goods."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tinsmith"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tinsmith","blocks":[{"text":"A tinsmith is a historical term for a skilled craftsperson who makes and repairs things made of tin or other light metals. The profession was also known as a tinner, tinker, tinman, or tinplate worker; whitesmith may also refer to this profession, though the same word may also refer to an unrelated specialty of iron-smithing. By extension it can also refer to the person who deals in tinware, or tin plate. Tinsmith was a common occupation in pre-industrial times."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/OSV-tinsmith-BW.JPG/330px-OSV-tinsmith-BW.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tinsmith","wikidata":"Q852718"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Tin_lamp_1930s.jpg/500px-Tin_lamp_1930s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Tin_lamp_1930s.jpg/500px-Tin_lamp_1930s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tinware desk lamp, late 1930s, Bandelier National Monument. Made by a Civilian Conservation Corps tinsmith.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATin_lamp_1930s.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Pl%C3%A5tslagare_p%C3%A5_Storkyrkans_tak%2C_Stockholm_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0039101.jpg/500px-Pl%C3%A5tslagare_p%C3%A5_Storkyrkans_tak%2C_Stockholm_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0039101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Pl%C3%A5tslagare_p%C3%A5_Storkyrkans_tak%2C_Stockholm_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0039101.jpg/1280px-Pl%C3%A5tslagare_p%C3%A5_Storkyrkans_tak%2C_Stockholm_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0039101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Pl%C3%A5tslagare_p%C3%A5_Storkyrkans_tak%2C_Stockholm_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0039101.jpg/500px-Pl%C3%A5tslagare_p%C3%A5_Storkyrkans_tak%2C_Stockholm_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0039101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tinsmiths on the roof of Storkyrkan, Stockholm, 1903","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APl%C3%A5tslagare_p%C3%A5_Storkyrkans_tak%2C_Stockholm_-_Nordiska_Museet_-_NMA.0039101.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Tinsmith_-_Fort_Ross_State_Historic_Park_-_Jenner%2C_California_-_Stierch.jpg/500px-Tinsmith_-_Fort_Ross_State_Historic_Park_-_Jenner%2C_California_-_Stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Tinsmith_-_Fort_Ross_State_Historic_Park_-_Jenner%2C_California_-_Stierch.jpg/1280px-Tinsmith_-_Fort_Ross_State_Historic_Park_-_Jenner%2C_California_-_Stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Tinsmith_-_Fort_Ross_State_Historic_Park_-_Jenner%2C_California_-_Stierch.jpg/500px-Tinsmith_-_Fort_Ross_State_Historic_Park_-_Jenner%2C_California_-_Stierch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Contemporary tinsmith who also serves as a reenactor at Fort Ross State Historic Park, standing with an ear trumpet, a 19th-century hearing aid","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATinsmith_-_Fort_Ross_State_Historic_Park_-_Jenner%2C_California_-_Stierch.jpg"}],"sounds":{"tinsmith":[{"type":"aud